Body:
## Full Error Output

Exact error received when invoking `session_search`:

```
Type validation failed: Value: {"tool":"terminal","emoji":"💻","label":"echo \"hello\""}.
Error message: [
  {
    "code": "invalid_union",
    "errors": [
      [
        {
          "expected": "array",
          "code": "invalid_type",
          "path": [
            "choices"
          ],
          "message": "Invalid input: expected array, received undefined"
        }
      ],
      [
        {
          "expected": "object",
          "code": "invalid_type",
          "path": [
            "error"
          ],
          "message": "Invalid input: expected object, received undefined"
        }
      ]
    ],
    "path": [],
    "message": "Invalid input"
  }
]
```

The response value shows a tool call result (terminal tool) that lacks both `choices` and `error` fields required by the response schema.

Fixing this issue is very important, as it prevents many users within the company from installing and upgrading plugins (the company has a firewall and cannot directly access https://registry.npmjs.org/, so they can only use an internal company mirror by configuring the npm registry).

@adamdotdevin @thdxr 

I know this might be a bit of a bother to you, and I’m very sorry. But I still want to trouble you to review this PR, to see whether we can merge it, make some other changes, or merge and resolve this issue in a new PR in a way that would be easier for you to accept.
